---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { pages } from '../i18n/en'
import { href, REPORT_URL } from '../lib/paths'

const P = pages.aboutPage
---

<Base title={P.title} description={P.description} breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: href() }, { name: 'About', href: href('about') }]}>
  <article class="prose-site max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold">{P.h1}</h1>
    <p class="text-lg muted">
      Every exam season, applicants get stuck on one line in a notification: “photo 20–50 KB, signature 10–20 KB”. Many end up paying a cyber café to do it.
      SahiSize does it on your phone, for free, and your files never leave it.
    </p>
    <h2>Independent</h2>
    <p>
      SahiSize is not connected to IBPS, SBI, SSC, UPSC, RRB, NTA, the Ministry of External Affairs, the Income Tax Department or any other body. Their names are
      used only to say which rules a preset follows.
    </p>
    <h2>Where the rules come from</h2>
    <p>
      Each preset is checked against the official notification, and its page shows the source and the date it was checked. Rules change with every notification,
      so always compare with yours. If you spot a difference, please <a href={REPORT_URL} rel="noopener">report it</a> and include a link to the notice.
    </p>
    <h2>Free</h2>
    <p>No sign-up, no limits, no ads, no watermark.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
